WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.798 --> 00:00:03.030
- [Reporter] Explosions
and fires in Crimea

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:07.560
have destroyed military
equipment, frightened beach goers,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.160
and prompted thousands of
residents to evacuate to Russia.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.500
After more than eight years
under Moscow's control,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.891
scenes of war have returned to Crimea.

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:19.558
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.538
- [Reporter] For several recent incidents,

00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:25.950
Ukraine hasn't claimed responsibility,

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.680
but Russia's operations have
been seriously disrupted

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.500
as Ukraine increasingly
focuses on striking facilities

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.570
and supplies behind Russian lines.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.760
- Actually, what they're doing
is part of a broader strategy

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.898
which is to try to squeeze the Russians

00:00:37.898 --> 00:00:40.320
out of the south of the country.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.000
- [Reporter] So as the
war enters a new phase

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.580
and President Zelensky vows
to take back the territory

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.830
at the heart of Russia's operations,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.780
here's why Crimea has emerged
as an important battleground.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.310
Russia's military seized Crimea,

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.400
which is internationally
recognized as Ukrainian territory,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.660
in 2014.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.060
Since then, Moscow has
built military bases

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.209
and weapons stores on the peninsula.

00:01:02.209 --> 00:01:05.876
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.290
- [Reporter] When Russia invaded
Ukraine in late February,

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.270
those hubs became important locations

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:18.840
from where Moscow could deploy
forces and top up supplies.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.110
- In the early days of
the war, Crimea was used

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.870
as a jump off point for Russia's military.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.130
- [Reporter] Russia's initial strategy

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.780
was a multi-directional invasion

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.590
with the goal of capture and
keep, but after that failed,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.240
fighting shifted to Eastern
and Southern Ukraine.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.380
- Since then, it's Crimea
that's been kind of a rear base

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.470
for Russian armed forces who are occupying

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.990
the south of Ukraine.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.771
Ukraine is now attempting
to push those forces out.

00:01:46.771 --> 00:01:47.604
(explosion booming)

00:01:47.604 --> 00:01:48.930
- [Reporter] Since taking control of parts

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.550
of Eastern Ukraine in July,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.890
Russia's forces have appeared to slow down

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.260
and Ukraine has repeatedly
hit occupied areas

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.360
with targeted strikes
on key infrastructure

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.343
that was being used by the invaders.

00:02:00.297 --> 00:02:02.760
- Ukraine, it thinks it
can't take the Russians on

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.870
in a tank battle.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.160
So they're being clever about it.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.040
Their aim is to degrade the Russians.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.170
The Ukrainian official said to me,

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:13.290
it's like 1,000 stings from a bee

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.100
in order to disable Russian capabilities,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.640
their ability to wage
war and demoralize them

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.740
and force them to withdraw.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.380
- [Reporter] Crimea is
now key to that strategy.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.510
A blast at a Russian airbase on August 9th

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.980
destroyed several war planes,

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.200
according to Western
intelligence officials.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.000
And as seen in these satellite images

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.590
that contradicted Moscow's claim

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.810
that no war planes were lost.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.640
Russia blamed an ammunition explosion,

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.910
and Ukraine didn't take
responsibility for the damage.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.920
But the blast had consequences.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.620
Russia relocated some planes
and aircraft to its mainland,

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.650
according to Ukrainian
military intelligence.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.150
A week after the airbase was hit,

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.910
explosions at an ammunition
depot damaged rail tracks

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.400
and power lines,
complicating Russia's efforts

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.310
to transport ammunition
and other supplies.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:02.880
Ukrainian officials said the
attack was indeed Ukrainian,

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.040
and Russian officials blamed saboteurs

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.630
in their first official acknowledgement

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.493
of a major attack on the peninsula.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.940
Still, that doesn't
necessarily mean Ukraine

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.683
is about to retake Crimea.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.550
- Certainly Crimea eventually is a target,

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.367
but the Ukrainians are going
about it very methodically,

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.950
piece by piece.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.990
- [Reporter] Russian diplomats
didn't respond to a request

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.540
for comment about the effects
of what's happening in Crimea

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.010
on Moscow's campaign.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.080
But as a new phase starts in the conflict,

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.450
the peninsula is at the
center of Ukraine's efforts

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.340
to show that it can damage Russia's army

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.663
where it didn't expect it.

